   ],
   "type": "orderedList"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "general",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Adding Two Random Variables",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Deriving an expression for the likelihood for the sum of two random variables requires an interesting insight. If your random variables are discrete then the probability that ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X + Y = n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " is the sum of mutually exclusive cases where ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X = 0 \\text{ and } Y = n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X = 1 \\text{ and } Y = n - 1"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " etc. In fact all of the mutually exclusive cases can be enumerated in a sum:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Def: General Rule for the Convolution of Discrete Variables ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\p(X + Y = n) = \\sum_{i=-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\p(X = i, Y = n- i)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If the random variables are independent you can further decompose the term ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\p(X = i, Y = n- i)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Let's expand on some of the mutually exclusive cases where ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X+Y=n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "sourceBytes": 1232,
    "sourceSha256": "72b2f34e597b4648a2e81938be207bd40f28f7c0f8596964ccba4be3eddfaa25"
   },
   "type": "interactive-demo"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Consider the sum of two independent dice. Let ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " be the outcome of each dice. Here is the probability mass function for the sum ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X + Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Let's use this context to practice deriving the sum of two variables, in this case ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\p(X + Y = n)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", starting with the General Rule for the Convolution of Discrete  Random Variables. We start by considering values of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " between 2 and 7. In this range ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\p(X = i, Y = n- i) = \\frac{1}{36}"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " for all values of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " between 1 and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n-1"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". There is exactly one outcome of the two dice where ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X = i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y = n - i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". For values of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " outside this range ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n- i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " is not a valid dice outcome and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\p(X = i, Y = n- i) = 0"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n\\p&(X + Y = n) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\p(X = i, Y = n- i) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\p(X = i, Y = n- i) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{i=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{36}\\\\\n&= \\frac{n-1}{36}\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "For values of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " greater than 7 we could use the same approach, though different values of ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "i"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " would make ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\p(X = i, Y = n- i)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " non-zero.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "This derivation for a general rule has a continuous equivalent:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n&f(X+Y = n) = \\int_{i=-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(X = n-i, Y=i) di\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "poissons",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Sum of Independent Poissons",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For any two Poisson random variables: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\Poi(\\lambda_1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y \\sim \\Poi(\\lambda_2)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " the sum of those two random variables is another Poisson: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X + Y \\sim \\Poi(\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". This holds even when ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\lambda_1"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " is not the same as ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\lambda_2"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "How could we prove the above claim?",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Example derivation:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nP(Z = n) \n&= P(X + Y = n) \\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\p(X = k, Y = n- k) && \\text{(Convolution)}\\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty} P(X = k) P(Y = n - k) && \\text{(Independence)}\\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^n P(X = k) P(Y = n - k) &&\\text{(Range of X and Y)}\\\\\n&= \\sum_{k=0}^n e^{-\\lambda_1} \\frac{\\lambda_1^k}{k!} e^{-\\lambda_2} \\frac{\\lambda_2^{n-k}}{(n-k)!} && \\text{(Poisson PMF)} \\\\\n&= e^{- (\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2)} \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{\\lambda_1^k \\lambda_2^{n-k}}{k!(n-k)!} \\\\\n&= \\frac{ e^{- (\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2)}}{n!} \\sum_{k=0}^n \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\lambda_1^k \\lambda_2^{n-k} \\\\\n&= \\frac{ e^{- (\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2)}}{n!} (\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2)^n && \\text{(Binomial theorem)}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Note that the Binomial Theorem (which we did not cover in this class, but is often used in contexts like expanding polynomials) says that for two numbers ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "a"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "b"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and positive integer ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ", ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "(a+b)^n = \\sum_{k=0}^n \\binom{n}{k} a^k b^{n-k}"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "binomials",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Sum of Independent Binomials with equal ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "p"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For any two independent Binomial random variables with the same \"success\" probability ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "p"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ": ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\Bin(n_1,p)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y \\sim \\Bin(n_2,p)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " the sum of those two random variables is another binomial: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X + Y \\sim \\Bin(n_1 + n_2,p)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "This result hopefully makes sense. The convolution is the number of successes across ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "Y"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ". Since each trial has the same probability of success, and there are now ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "n_1 + n_2"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " trials, which are all independent, the convolution is simply a new Binomial. This rule does not hold when the two Binomial random variables have different parameters ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "p"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ".",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "normals",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Sum of Independent Normals",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "For any two independent Normal random variables ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_1,\\sigma_1^2)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_2,\\sigma_2^2)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " the sum of those two random variables is another Normal: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": ""
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nX +Y \\sim \\mathcal{N}(\\mu_1 + \\mu_2,\\sigma_1^2 + \\sigma_2^2)\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Again, this only holds when the two Normals are independent.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "id": "uniforms",
    "level": "2",
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Sum of Independent Uniforms",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "heading"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " are independent uniform random variables where ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\Uni(0,1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y \\sim \\Uni(0,1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ":",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\nf(X+Y=n) = \n\\begin{cases}\nn,   & \\text{if } 0 < n \\le 1,\\\\\n2-n, & \\text{if } 1 < n \\le 2,\\\\\n0,   & \\text{otherwise.}\n\\end{cases}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        },
        {
         "type": "italic"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Example derivation",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ": ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Calculate the PDF of ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X + Y"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " for independent uniform random variables ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "X \\sim \\Uni(0,1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "Y \\sim \\Uni(0,1)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": "? First plug in the equation for general convolution of independent random variables:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    f(X+Y=n) \n    &= \\int_{i=0}^{1} f(X=n-i, Y=i)\\,di\\\\\n    &= \\int_{i=0}^{1} f(X=n-i)f(Y=i)\\,di && \\text{Independence}\\\\\n     &= \\int_{i=0}^{1} f(X=n-i)\\,di && \\text{Because } f(Y=y) = 1\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "It turns out that is not the easiest thing to integrate. By trying a few different values of ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " in the range ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "[0,2]"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " we can observe that the PDF we are trying to calculate is discontinuous at the point ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n=1"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and thus will be easier to think about as two cases: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n < 1"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " and ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "n > 1"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". If we calculate ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "f(X+Y=n)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " for both cases and correctly constrain the bounds of the integral we get simple closed forms for each case:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    f(X+Y=n) = \\begin{cases} n &\\text{if } 0 < n \\leq 1 \\\\ \n2-n & \\text{if } 1 < n \\leq 2 \\\\\n0 & \\text{else} \\end{cases}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  }
 ],
 "type": "doc"
}
